  "faq": [
    {
      "question": "What is the best port wine cellar to visit in Porto?",
      "answer": "Graham's and Taylor's are the most recommended on Reddit. Graham's has the best terrace views over Porto, while Taylor's offers the most comprehensive tasting experience. Both are in Vila Nova de Gaia, across the river from Porto's old town."
    },
    {
      "question": "How much does a wine tasting cost in Porto?",
      "answer": "Port cellar tours with tasting run €15–€25 per person. Wine bars typically charge €3–€8 per glass for good Portuguese wine and €5–€15 for port. A full tasting flight at a wine bar is usually €12–€25. Porto is excellent value compared to other European wine cities."
    },
    {
      "question": "Should I visit Vila Nova de Gaia or stay in Porto for wine?",
      "answer": "Both. Vila Nova de Gaia (across the river) is where all the major port cellars are located — Graham's, Taylor's, Sandeman, etc. Porto's old town has better independent wine bars for Douro table wines and natural wines. Plan a day for each side of the river."
    },
    {
      "question": "Is port wine the only wine worth drinking in Porto?",
      "answer": "Absolutely not. The Douro Valley produces world-class red and white table wines, and Portugal's Vinho Verde region is nearby. Many Reddit users say the non-port Douro reds were their biggest surprise. Port is essential to try, but don't miss the table wines."
    }
